{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedGraph"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Edges and their identity."}]},{"type":"text","text":" Edges may repeat (parallel edges) unless the representation says"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"otherwise. Each edge, every copy included, has a position in "},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and that position is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge’s identity: "},{"code":"outEdges(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" lists the positions of the edges leaving a vertex, so an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"algorithm can tell parallel edges apart and keep per-edge values (weights, capacities, flow)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keyed by "},{"code":"Edges.Index","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"code":"source(ofEdgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"target(ofEdgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" read an edge’s endpoints"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"without the cost of "},{"code":"edges[i]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Positions are valid until the graph is mutated."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Counting.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Every count and neighborhood counts each edge once, so a repeated edge counts once"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"per copy: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successors(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" lists a target once per edge to it, in the same order as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outEdges(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outDegree(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is the length of either. For a simple graph these are the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"set definitions."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vertex indices."}]},{"type":"text","text":" A representation with dense vertex indices reports "},{"code":"vertexIndexBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"then "},{"code":"vertexIndex(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" maps its vertices one-to-one onto "},{"code":"0..<vertexIndexBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"algorithms can keep per-vertex state in arrays instead of dictionaries (Boost’s "},{"code":"vertex_index","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"petgraph’s "},{"code":"NodeCompactIndexable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). Indices are valid until the graph is mutated."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"successorIndices(ofIndex:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" gives adjacency directly in index space, and "},{"code":"outEdges(ofIndex:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the out-edges without looking the vertex up. A representation with dense edge indices also"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reports "},{"code":"edgeIndexBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and then "},{"code":"edgeIndex(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" maps edge positions one-to-one onto"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"0..<edgeIndexBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (Boost’s "},{"code":"edge_index","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", petgraph’s "},{"code":"EdgeIndexable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), so per-edge values"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(weights, flow) can live in arrays."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Laws."}]},{"type":"text","text":" Every conformer satisfies:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"vertexCount == vertices.count","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the vertices are distinct, and every edge’s endpoints are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices; ","type":"text"},{"code":"edgeCount == edges.count","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For every vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outEdges(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":" lists each position of an edge leaving "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":" exactly"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"source(ofEdgeAt: e) == v"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"target(ofEdgeAt: e) == edges[e].target"},{"type":"text","text":" for each;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successors(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":" is their targets in the same order; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outDegree(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":" is their count."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The out-degrees sum to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeCount"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contains(edge:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is true exactly for the edges in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contains"},{"type":"text","text":" is false (and does not trap) for anything absent."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Asking again gives the same answer.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"With vertex indices, ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is in index order: ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertex(atIndex: i)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the ","type":"text"},{"code":"i","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"th vertex,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so an algorithm that visits vertices in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order can walk ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<vertexIndexBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"With vertex indices, "},{"code":"successorIndices(ofIndex: vertexIndex(of: v))","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"successors(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" mapped through "},{"code":"vertexIndex(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", in the same order, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"outEdges(ofIndex: vertexIndex(of: v))","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"outEdges(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; for every position "},{"code":"e","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"sourceIndex(ofEdgeAt: e)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"targetIndex(ofEdgeAt: e)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" are the indices of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"source(ofEdgeAt: e)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"target(ofEdgeAt: e)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"With edge indices, ","type":"text"},{"code":"edgeIndexBound == edgeCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"edgeIndex(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is one-to-one onto","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<edgeIndexBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is in index order: the ","type":"text"},{"code":"k","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"th position of ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"edgeIndex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"k","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (so ","type":"text"},{"code":"undirected","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which forwards both, keeps ","type":"text"},{"code":"Graph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s law of the same name).","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Defaults.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Members with default implementations are requirements, not extension methods, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a representation’s faster version is the one generic code calls. A type that wraps another"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph generically (a view, a relabeling) must implement every requirement by forwarding to its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"base: a default chosen for the wrapper would ignore the base’s faster member."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The protocol has no mutation: mutation belongs to concrete types, and the refinement"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MutableDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" (Boost’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MutableGraph"},{"type":"text","text":") gives wrappers the few hooks they need to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"mutate a base generically. It does not refine"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":"; representations are "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":" when their vertices are, and algorithms that cross"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"isolation ask for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph & Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of directed edges between"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Associated-Types","title":"Associated Types","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/OutEdges","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/SuccessorIndices","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Successors","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertex","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertices-swift.associatedtype"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/edgeCount","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/edgeIndexBound","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/edges-swift.property","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/vertexCount","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/vertexIndexBound","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/vertices-swift.property"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/contains(_:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/contains(edge:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/edgeIndex(of:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/outDegree(of:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/outDegree(ofIndex:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/outEdges(of:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/outEdges(ofIndex:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/source(ofEdgeAt:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/sourceIndex(ofEdgeAt:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/successorIndices(ofIndex:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/successors(of:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/target(ofEdgeAt:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/targetIndex(ofEdgeAt:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/vertex(atIndex:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/vertexIndex(of:)"]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"inheritedBy","kind":"relationships","title":"Inherited By","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/SparselyIndexedDirectedGraph"]},{"type":"conformingTypes","kind":"re